data/: the cartridge's data as typed tables (plan section 3). Places live
only in the .c files here, behind data_internal.h. Checked by
tools/data_check.py ROM (every range against the ROM, every reader against a
second reading of the ROM; PLANT=1 shows it can fail).

Readers (2026-11-19), 8 tables:
  sound_tables.c  the 55-entry upload table at $85:8000 and its lists (42 used: config/aladdin/spclists.csv)
  video_tables.c  the quarter sine ($82:87D4, 64 steps); the palette loads ($84:C000, 98);
                  the packed-graphics format; the level graphics lists ($80:DF98, 66 levels);
                  the unpack sets ($80:F039, 50)
  input_tables.c  the demos' pad scripts ($84:F700)

Not readable from cart.dat as it is (stage 0's assets.csv leaves out every
byte the S-CPU runs, and 8,972 of them, in 177 runs, are also read as data
by the traces):
  - AnimSetGraphicsUnpack's entries at $82:AC18 (a word per animation set)
    lie inside the routine at $82:AC10; cart.dat has zeros there. No reader
    until those bytes are kept.
  - The other runs (most in $80:8000-$80:B56E, and single bytes after task
    calls) are listed in the session notes (code-read-as-data.txt); which of
    them the native game needs is settled by the code that reads them.

Record comment that is wrong, found here: video/unpack.c's LEVEL_GFX says
bank $81; LevelGraphicsLoad runs with DB = $80 and the table is $80:DF98.
